  "overall_verdict": "MARGINAL",
  "interpretation": "GPR proxies based on gold and oil price momentum provide negligible incremental information for volatility prediction beyond VIX. This reinforces the VIX sufficiency finding (J3/J4/J8/J13): VIX already captures geopolitical fear through options markets faster than commodity price movements. Gold and oil react to geopolitical events, but options implied volatility reacts first. The GPR_Divergence proxy (GLD-SPY spread) shows the strongest individual signal but is subsumed by VIX. VT overlays with GPR produce negligible Sharpe improvement (<0.01). This is the 24th+ confirmation of VIX as the sufficient statistic for volatility targeting at daily/weekly horizons."
}